  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A student investigates the variation of current <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> with potential difference <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> for a thermistor. The results are plotted on a log-log graph. The data produce a straight line with negative gradient. What does this indicate?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p>Resistance is constant</p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> is directly proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> is inversely proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I\"></span> is proportional to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V^{-n}\"></span>, with <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n &gt; 0\"></span></p></li></ol>"
